1	/**
2	 * Mapping a synthesized journey onto the shape the generic real-app runner
3	 * consumes.
4	 *
5	 * The mapping is where the honesty rule becomes structural rather than
6	 * editorial. A hand-authored journey returns `assertions` in prose because a
7	 * person watched the application do the thing they wrote down. Synthesis
8	 * watched nothing, so what it returns is drawn entirely from the closed
9	 * vocabulary in `vocabulary.ts`, and every string is passed back through that
10	 * file's guard on the way out — a synthesized journey physically cannot return
11	 * a bare pass verb, because the only strings it can build refuse to contain one.
12	 *
13	 * The emission is deliberately in two halves.
14	 *
15	 * {@link emitSynthesizedJourney} produces what is true the moment the journey
16	 * is derived: how many gestures it declares, how many constructs the reader
17	 * declined to express, which routes it will visit. Nothing there is a claim
18	 * about the application.
19	 *
20	 * {@link completeSynthesizedJourney} produces what is true after a run has
21	 * measured it: routes reached out of routes declared, selectors found present
22	 * out of selectors declared. That half is the runner's to call, and it is
23	 * separate precisely so the derivation cannot state a measurement it has not
24	 * taken.
